OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786396755
OL,3,C'More angry than ever': Mother of PC
OL,4,CHarper calls for Burnham meeting
OL,6,FAround 5,000 people are expected to be
OL,7,Freleased early under sentencing
OL,8,Fchanges, down from an initial estimate
OL,9,Fof 6,000 after some exemptions were
OL,10,Fannounced as part of an urgent
OL,11,Fgovernment review of the scheme.
OL,13,FThe measures, which are due to begin
OL,14,Fin October, are designed to tackle
OL,15,Fovercrowding in prisons.
OL,17,FAileen O'Connor, who chairs the body
OL,18,Fthat represents officers in PC
OL,19,FHarper's former force, Thames Valley
OL,20,FPolice, also chimed in on the
OL,21,Fgovernment's statement.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30208
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786396755
OL,3,C'More angry than ever': Mother of PC
OL,4,CHarper calls for Burnham meeting
OL,6,F"The public are speaking loudly and
OL,7,Fclearly," she said.
OL,9,F"They agree with us that the
OL,10,FGovernment are firmly on the wrong
OL,11,Fside of this.
OL,13,F"What they are doing is indefensible.
OL,14,FAnd they simply cannot defend it.
OL,16,F"They must listen. The Prime Minister
OL,17,Fmust listen."
OL,19,FShe added: "If you kill a police
OL,20,Fofficer there should be no early
OL,21,Frelease. No ifs. No buts."
OL,26,@qD@AOUuD@AOUxD@AOUyD@MO]{D@LOU}D@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/12
